  "limitations": [
    "n <= 16 variables are solved exactly in milliseconds by brute force, so no quantum advantage is claimed.",
    "QAOA with the standard X mixer spends most of its effort on the sum x = k penalty: P(optimal) stays a small multiple of uniform guessing at p <= 3, and results depend on the penalty weight (see the sweep).",
    "The QAOA placement is decoded from the exact statevector distribution (simulator-only). The hardware-realistic most-frequent-shot decoding (QAOA-shots) is far noisier and is reported separately.",
    "QAOA-best-sample (best of 4096 shots over 495 valid states) is close to brute force and is not evidence of quantum quality on its own.",
    "Survivor likelihood is a hand-defined proxy (0.45 flood + 0.35 built-up + 0.20 edge + noise), not real survivor data, so the CNN learns a known function.",
    "The pairwise radio reward does not guarantee a connected relay chain to base; the post-hoc connectivity rate is reported per method.",
    "The agent is a keyword parser and is brittle to unusual phrasing; a human confirmation step is needed in practice.",
    "Simulator and simple noise-model results do not predict real-hardware behaviour.",
    "Scaling beyond 16 qubits was not tested.",
    "Default radio range is 2.25 cells, not 1.5: with R = 1.5 the radio matrix equals the 8-neighbour overlap matrix and the overlap/connectivity terms partly cancel."
  ],
